  "drivers": [],
  "summary": "Picabo Street is a retired American alpine skiing legend whose commercial marketability relies on her immense historic authority, uniquely compelling personal narrative, and active presence in high-profile sports media. As an Olympic gold and silver medalist and a pioneer for American women's downhill skiing, Street's legacy is firmly cemented. Her cultural relevance has experienced a powerful resurgence, driven by the 2022 Peacock documentary 'PICABO' (co-directed by Lindsey Vonn) and her high-profile debut as NBC's hill reporter and analyst for the Milano Cortina 2026 Olympic Winter Games, where her broadcast activations with icons like Snoop Dogg gained widespread traction. While her personal direct social media audience remains comparatively small, her broader narrative power—anchored by a legendary name, extreme resilience, and overcoming severe physical and personal trauma—commands significant prestige. She maintains solid commercial proof through premium speaking engagements and brand partnerships for her Picabo Street Academy. A past 2015 domestic incident was fully dismissed in court and has been transparently integrated into her comeback narrative, minimizing brand-safety risks. Her marketability today operates at a high level as a premium legacy endorser, commentator, and motivational authority.",
